# Crease (MVP)

Crease is a mobile-first Progressive Web App for **Ranches Thunders**.

People install it on iPhone or Android. The UI must feel like a native utility app and strictly follow the Stitch Athletic Precision design.

## Roles (exactly two)

- **Admin** — team admin; drawn only from the player pool; can also play and vote
- **Player** — active squad member

No Captain, Vice Captain, Coach, or other roles in MVP.

## Access rule

A user must be an **active team member** (added by Admin). Otherwise every screen returns access denied.

## MVP scope

- Single team: **Ranches Thunders**
- Mobile OTP login (dummy OTP for local/dev) + **KMSI** until explicit sign-out
- Weekend match creation (Sat / Sun / both)
- Warmup vs Tournament matches
- Auto availability + carpool polls on confirm
- WhatsApp group + PWA push notifications (scheduled + event-driven)
- Weekend fee settlement (UPI, UTR, compressed screenshot)
- Team fund tracker, expenses, manual ₹300 contribution asks

## Out of MVP

- Multi-team product surface
- Extra roles
- Full analytics / reports suite
- Automated fund contribution collection (manual notify only)

## Guiding principles

- Mobile first, PWA first
- Stitch design fidelity
- Clean architecture (UI → Hook → Service → Repository → Supabase)
- No duplicated business logic
- Services enforce authorization; UI only hides actions
